{"skill":{"slug":"notebooklm-skill","displayName":"Notebooklm"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769506823210,"changelog":"notebooklm-skill v0.1.0\n\n- Initial release introducing integration with Google NotebookLM for source-grounded, citation-backed research queries.\n- Provides persistent authentication, browser automation, and robust notebook/document management via a Python script interface.\n- Features Smart Discovery for notebook metadata, minimizing the need for manual data entry.\n- Strongly enforces use of a wrapper script (run.py) for consistent environment setup and dependency management.\n- Includes critical follow-up and synthesis workflow for comprehensive, accurate responses.\n- Stores all data locally with security in mind; configuration options via `.env` supported.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"AUTHENTICATION.md","size":5729,"sha256":"2b1dbabbe732d011203debf38ed4af41bfb518d30c43bece928dfd45daa6e350","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","size":1774,"sha256":"04c7d84879cd07d7ac2012fb190ea3587bf91515e1af7b8a57ea00a11ddf03c2","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"README.md","size":15901,"sha256":"1c009fc025e0bcff9fa9c0126644d60011f38f50a4f61dcfd9f74a4df050b450","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":9442,"sha256":"8fcfe1aa04523483c1d1a5aa10835bc796228d2de9a66460a767bf2d6ed7432e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/api_reference.md","size":7630,"sha256":"bb4b57b7f39f213961be77fedf83fd5a8ebe30746a6d212e5c36ac1d64bb8eac","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/troubleshooting.md","size":8994,"sha256":"b32709f82c66564ed5c1948f37f80a7d7b3f49a250e10ffb37e579733a4a0b45","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/usage_patterns.md","size":9574,"sha256":"be990a67326e1f1612e7a00cca6a6a2263593dd7a623a137194b87f55446a650","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":325,"sha256":"001076a8c9bc206a8dc6556f5bcb5fcb1864494cca2bdf698160b001923a8aa1","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/__init__.py","size":2627,"sha256":"b8ccc9d7d23f336fb570f946bd015367a73cc27d5eef7f5fc2eb74f1503a9e46","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/ask_question.py","size":8196,"sha256":"29ee6d8744783ef81bf09145ad64bfa1f7f7aff217b0de1ba21e0f4c80bda1b6","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/auth_manager.py","size":11544,"sha256":"2494af0da219bad907b097d26f663eb2557ee5f1db25b8a926d8945b1c1e9d30","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/browser_session.py","size":8725,"sha256":"6c2de8e83be0e2843b27d502744978f45c563cb8334f109938ac557e27f78496","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/browser_utils.py","size":3525,"sha256":"98172e3e02e42348093ec6e9ddfa754ba3fa2603ad2d188fc9838ca27e44a39a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/cleanup_manager.py","size":9777,"sha256":"0a85a8d0164eb3ae7aa15356af814a28717cfc1000a43f0291a2a1946401d7e0","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/config.py","size":1228,"sha256":"e614bb83a1b2fa230a9848b6480e6ff62fd3d7e37aee4349f40298e7e582b65b","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/notebook_manager.py","size":13843,"sha256":"759384d94eabab346e9c4da73ee968d68277498d8ec19d261554a63ec3ac0238","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/run.py","size":2967,"sha256":"7f81301b8dde236a5a15a01f4db9530e5cd90bd2bcc1d7b0eb13bc58da81d79f","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/setup_environment.py","size":7168,"sha256":"895c9055577e8e0bad8801681ad9becd9ff6b6bb72107b6b359c1cf8512f0ac0","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2885,"sha256":"76dfa4800b2b119c378c3cdbc11bc5acff58771e81b841f6281a3552283a44d1","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789022137172,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"1504836e0f6f29f5cbbe365d96333bb834fb4c4d78e6fb9128256fb8f5ec1b23","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/1504836e0f6f29f5cbbe365d96333bb834fb4c4d78e6fb9128256fb8f5ec1b23","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: notebooklm-skill\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its extensive use of high-risk capabilities, even though the stated intent appears functional. Key indicators include: 1) Browser automation with anti-detection features (e.g., `StealthUtils`, `BROWSER_ARGS` in `scripts/browser_utils.py` and `scripts/config.py`), which, while explained as necessary for reliable interaction with Google, are commonly associated with malicious bots. 2) Local storage of sensitive Google authentication session tokens (`state.json`) in `~/.claude/skills/notebooklm/data/browser_state/` as confirmed by `scripts/auth_manager.py` and `AUTHENTICATION.md`. 3) Significant use of prompt injection against the AI agent in `SKILL.md` and `scripts/ask_question.py` (e.g., 'CRITICAL: Add Command - Smart Discovery', 'EXTREMELY IMPORTANT: Is that ALL you need to know?'), instructing the agent to perform specific actions and decision-making, which is a high-risk technique even if used for benign purposes here. 4) The skill installs a full browser (Google Chrome) via `patchright install chrome` as seen in `scripts/setup_environment.py` and `requirements.txt`, and uses `subprocess.run` for various system commands, granting it powerful execution capabilities.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160117557},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":49,"checkedAt":1789022137172},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill mostly does what it says, but it stores Google browser session data and gives the agent broad, risky browser and command behavior that users should review before installing.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill launches a persistent Chrome profile with Google session cookies, disables the Chrome sandbox, and accepts NotebookLM URLs without validating the origin before navigation.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation is a normal local skill clone and first use creates a skill-local virtual environment, installs pinned Python dependencies, and installs a browser through Patchright; this is disclosed but requires network/package trust.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"SKILL.md requires the agent to stop, analyze, and repeatedly ask follow-up questions, and ask_question.py appends that instruction to every answer, blurring the boundary between retrieved content and local control instructions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Authentication cookies and localStorage are persisted in data/browser_state/state.json and a Chrome profile without enforced restrictive permissions, and the artifact claims .gitignore protection although no .gitignore file is present.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The NotebookLM query, browser automation, persistent auth, and local notebook library features fit the stated purpose, but the skill also mixes agent-control text into NotebookLM answers and documents account switching for rate-limit workarounds.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with local browser automation using your Google account. Prefer a dedicated Google account, keep the skill directory private, avoid storing it in synced or shared folders, verify NotebookLM URLs before use, and treat cleanup/remove commands as data-deleting operations.","findings":"[T01] unexpected: The appended follow-up reminder is artifact-backed and materially risky because it is agent-directed control text added to retrieved answers and reinforced as mandatory behavior.\n[T09] unexpected: The runner path traversal concern is supported: run.py and setup_environment.py build script paths from caller-controlled names without resolving or allowlisting them.\n[T09] unexpected: The URL navigation concern is supported: notebook URLs are stored and opened before origin validation, increasing risk with a persistent authenticated browser profile.\n[T09] expected: Persistent Google browser state is expected for this skill, but storing cookies/localStorage without explicit permission hardening is under-scoped for the sensitivity of the data.\n[TP4] expected: Library removal and cleanup are local maintenance functions aligned with notebook management, but the destructive effects are not consistently foregrounded next to every command.\n[TM1] expected: The direct library reset command is a troubleshooting step with a nearby backup command, but it is still a destructive local metadata deletion that should be handled cautiously.\n[OH1] unexpected: The cited subprocess examples pass arguments as a list and do not show shell, SQL, or HTML execution of model output; this finding was downgraded as unsupported by the inspected artifact.\n[SQP-2] expected: state.json and the browser profile intentionally retain authentication state, but users need clearer warnings that these files may contain reusable Google session material.\n[RA2] expected: The observed persistence is normal skill installation, a local virtual environment, and auth/library state; no cron job, startup hook, or backdoor persistence was found.\n[AS3] unexpected: The directory listing examples check the skill's install and data paths for troubleshooting, not peer skill contents or secrets.\n[LP3] expected: Shell, file, network, browser, and package-install capabilities are needed for the advertised workflow, but the artifact does not provide tight tool/path scoping.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The docs are inconsistent: they say there is no session persistence while separately documenting persistent browser/auth state.\n[SDI-1] expected: Auth, cleanup, and notebook library management are broader than simple querying but are disclosed in the skill description and supporting docs.\n[EA2] expected: Cleanup has preview and confirmation by default, but the documented --force option can skip the prompt for local data deletion.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Guidance to switch or use multiple Google accounts for rate limits is not needed for the core query workflow and may encourage service-limit evasion.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789022137172}}}}}